    action def DeliveryRunS385 {
        action storyP1PavedWritePath;
        verification storyP1PavedWritePathDoD : Test { :>> id = "a62a2a83-4ef1-484a-8c13-16cfb4793d47"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DELIVERED BACKLOG ITEMS: p1TieredDeny, p1BashMatcher, p1HumanChannel, p1ControlPlane, p1RulesWired, p1AuditHistoryCi, p1RedYield. THE TIERS (d0176), all run live on a strict scaffold: tier 1 hard-denies API-owned surfaces naming the sanctioned command; tier 2 asks on other .tracking writes; tier 3 is `keel override <path> --reason` - single-use (second write re-denied, proven), path-bound, 900s expiry, consumption recording an orient-visible obligation Issue ONE FILE PER FACT so recording never deadlocks on the file being repaired, with a local-ledger fallback on tracked-write failure. Control plane (d0179): .claude/settings.json, .githooks/, the output style, plus Bash core.hooksPath/deactivate/actor mutation route to ask with a recorded fact under strict - and the pure-shell test covers control-plane paths, so they are denied even with NO binary. THE MATCHER (d0176/d0178) tokenizes argv - a commit message DESCRIBING --no-verify is one quoted token and does not match (tested); unambiguous blocks: redirection/tee/sed -i into fact surfaces, --no-verify, SKIP_VALIDATE/SKIP_KEEL, core.hooksPath; keel-argv0 commands are exempt EXCEPT the never-exempt set DERIVED from write.rs's WRITE_OPS declared-attribute table (accept, apply-review, actor, enroll, deactivate) and any invocation carrying KEEL_ACTOR/--by/--judged-by naming a registered Person. HUMAN CHANNEL (d0178), three layers: the write layer refuses AI-kind and unregistered judges on accept_decision AND on method=confirmation results (unit-tested both ways: Person passes, AI refused, method=test unaffected); the channel layer refuses `keel accept` in agent-marked sessions without a TTY - PROVEN BY THIS SESSION REFUSING ITSELF, live; the matcher layer above. RULES WIRED (d0177): blocking rules gate hook stop, the pre-commit (self-build script + scaffolded const), and CI via the new `keel rules --enforce`; the scaffolded CI template's rules step activated; hook_stop now routes guards through run_all so the ACTIVATION FILTER applies - the proposal's cited bypass (a deactivated process's guard blocking turns) is dead. AUDIT (d0179/K15): CI runs keel audit-history over the pushed range; CLAUDE.md's never-rebase line softened to what is actually enforced. RED-YIELD (d0176): the Stop hook's second red pass still yields but records a tracked obligation (ledger fallback when the actor is unbound, so the yield record can never deepen the red it records). The self-build declares profile=guided: every detection runs and the fire-ledger accrues the D0180 evidence; blocking here is a future promotion decision citing it (K14). 220 tests; clippy 0; 41 guards ALL PASS."; }
        part storyP1PavedWritePathDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "12817c2b-64df-4b61-9187-83ce0885e664"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "894e394"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-21"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    }

    verification p1PavedWritePathRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "a2fda465-dbd8-40ac-a801-09d7ae5fd367"; :>> title = "Sprint 385 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-21"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "DoR. P1's seven chartered items, the P0-P1 chain being the one hard prerequisite path everything shares. The accepted decision texts (d0176-d0179) were read as the spec before any code. estimatedPoints=13."; }
